Why Were Web Workers Introduced?

Before Web Workers, all JavaScript code ran on the main thread.

Example:

for (let i = 0; i < 10000000000; i++) {
  // Heavy computation
}

While this loop runs:

Buttons stop responding
Scrolling becomes impossible
Animations freeze
The browser may show "Page Unresponsive"

To prevent this, Web Workers were introduced so that CPU-intensive tasks could run in the background without affecting the user interface.